# Alpha OS — PipeWire audio stack — Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (resolute)
# Provenance: names verified as exact matches against the resolute
# binary-amd64 Packages indexes on archive.ubuntu.com (released 23 Apr 2026).
#
# Signal chain:
#   applications -> libpulse (libpulse0, libpulse0t64 in universe runtime) ->
#   pipewire-pulse (PulseAudio protocol shim) -> PipeWire (pipewire) ->
#   ALSA (pipewire-alsa) / JACK (pipewire-jack), policy by WirePlumber.
#
# The standalone `pulseaudio` daemon IS installed (so legacy tools and
# pavucontrol work identically), but it is MASKED by a chroot hook so it can
# never race pipewire-pulse for the sound devices. Do not remove it here.
#
# NOTE: the `*-alsa` / `*-jack` PulseAudio module packages (pulseaudio-alsa,
# pulseaudio-jack) do not exist in resolute; `pulseaudio-module-jack` is the
# supported substitute. `pipewire-audio-client-modules` does not exist; use
# `pipewire-audio-client-libraries`.

pipewire
pipewire-bin
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
wireplumber
libspa-0.2-modules
libspa-0.2-modules-extra
pipewire-audio-client-libraries
pulseaudio
pulseaudio-utils
pulseaudio-module-bluetooth
pulseaudio-module-jack
libpulse0
pavucontrol
pavucontrol-qt
